<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-HANSA OPEN TO MERGER TALKS.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-HANSA OPEN TO MERGER TALKS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hansapank said on Tuesday it was open to starting merger talks with smaller banks in the Baltic countries to speed its present growth level.</p>
<p>&quot;We are ready to start discussing a common future with them (smaller banks),&quot; bank chairman Juri Mois told a news conference.</p>
<p>But he said there were no concrete plans at present.</p>
<p>As the bank has grown about two times per year since its establishment, its growth may speed up in the following year, Mois said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a feeling it may be quickened further,&quot; Mois said.</p>
<p>The bank also plans to raise its market share in Estonia to 29.5 percent at the end of this year from 25.3 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
